hey everybody welcome back to therm  learning my name is Heinrich and it's  great that all of you and they are ready  to watch my second video on this channel  I'm still super excited to have done  this at all and be able to share my  experience with you my experiences from  my background in business and management  so I thought long and hard about what  could be a good topic for this video and  I think one thing that many many many  new joiners and business struggle with  is behavior in meetings and what do I  mean by that what you can imagine most  corporations we have many many meetings  every day you probably meet with your  team leave them with other colleagues  from other departments you sit together  to discuss topics and make advancements  in the projects that you're pursuing and  to basically collect input from other  people you are working with and recently  a more junior colleague at my workplace  approached me and asked me about  specific Eva's topic he told me I'm like  you know I'm sitting in these meetings  very often I do not know what to say is  the right thing for me as a junior  colleague to say anything at all should  I just be there listen to the others  what is my role what am I expected to do  as a junior colleague in these meetings  and I could just very much relate to  that I clearly remember when I was a  rookie in consulting and I was sitting  in these first meetings with some senior  clients  I fed highly intimidated you're very  often not sitting there alone but then  there is your your your project you eat  your engagement manager there's a  partner from your consulting firm their  frequent leader might also be a junior  partner and then a whole bunch of  clients and then there was of course me  as well I know the junior consultant  knew on the team a rookie and I just  didn't have a clue what okay and I think  this is just the normal reaction that  many people have when they are facing  these kinds of situations so reflecting  on that 