 the meeting  organizer that is feasible and ask him  what do we actually want to take out of  the meeting and if you feel that  especially towards the end there's no  clear objective nor clear result towards  that goal that you want to achieve make  sure that actions are being taken right  sit together and really ask to each in  the room okay what are the things now  that we want to do what are the next  steps maybe walk up front go to a  flipchart write down what the next steps  are that are supposed to come out of  there ask the very simple question who  is supposed to do what until when and  really make sure that this is clear and  everybody is on the same page for that  because this is just the basics that  just need to be there after meeting for  two heaven had  any venue at all if this is not there  and was just a waste of time for  everybody and if other colleagues do not  understand this I do not see this in the  moment but you do then for the sake of  everybody step up and make sure that  these things are being clarified and  done of course here you need to be  careful for office politics depending on  the situation that you are in it might  be that this might seem inappropriate to  do as a junior colleague so here always  also ask your teamily for other  colleagues for feedback or maybe in the  very beginning observe or other people  are behaving just to make sure that you  do not break the kind of more implicit  rules of the organization's how  different people are supposed to behave  especially based on tenure and just what  the expectations of the other people are  to not be basically seen as an idiot by  the colleagues or just being seen as  rude this of course you should avoid so  yeah I think three neat tips that are  really crucial and important for you to  be successful in meetings as a junior  colleague first clarify your role  beforehand second in the meeting if  there is not another row that you are  assigned to be the number guy be sure  that 